sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor T as Trainer
    actor S as Student
    participant LC as liveclass-service
    participant BA as batch-service
    participant LK as LiveKit
    participant K as Kafka

    T->>BA: schedule a session (batch, time, mode)
    BA->>K: session-scheduled
    K->>LC: create live_session SCHEDULED

    T->>LC: POST /class-sessions/{id}/join
    LC->>BA: does this trainer teach the batch? (Feign, fails closed)
    LC->>LK: create room if missing
    LC->>LC: status SCHEDULED -> LIVE, token with host rights
    LC-->>T: LiveKit token (roomAdmin)
    T->>LK: connect (media goes direct)

    S->>LC: join
    LC->>BA: is the student enrolled in the batch?
    LC->>LC: RoomPermissions: mic / camera / screen allowed?
    LC-->>S: token carrying only the permitted sources
    S->>LK: connect

    LK-->>LC: signed webhook participant_joined / left
    LC->>LC: sum time in the room (reconnects added)

    opt Host changes a rule mid-class
        T->>LC: mute all / allow mic for one student
        LC->>LK: update publish permissions
    end

    opt Live question
        T->>LC: ask question
        LC->>LK: data message live-question
        S->>LC: answer (one per student)
        LC->>LC: auto-grade choice and short answers
    end

    T->>LC: End class (or sweep job settles an abandoned room)
    LC->>LC: status LIVE -> ENDED, close open questions, stop recording
    LC->>LC: attendance % = time in room / class length
    LC->>K: attendance-computed
    K->>BA: write register: PRESENT/LATE by threshold, ABSENT if never seen, keep manual marks
    BA->>K: attendance-marked
